---
title: Marry me chicken
servings: 4
tags: [italian, chicken, weeknight, quick]
time: 30 minutes
source: Marry Me Chicken by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/marry-me-chicken.html
---

Shake the @all-purpose flour{3%tbsp}, @salt{3/4%tsp} and
@black pepper{1/4%tsp} together in a #zip-top bag{}. Add the
@boneless skinless chicken breasts{1 1/4%lb}(4 thin-sliced), seal and shake to
coat.

Heat the @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} in a large #nonstick skillet{} over
medium-high heat. Cook the chicken ~{3%minutes} in all, turning once, until
lightly golden and cooked through. Set it on a plate.

Turn the heat to medium. Cook the @yellow onion{1}(small, finely chopped)
~{2%minutes} to ~{3%minutes}, until soft. Add the @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and
stir ~{30%seconds}, without letting it colour.

Stir in the @heavy cream{1%cup}, @chicken broth{1%cup},
@sun-dried tomatoes{1/3%cup}(oil-packed, drained, finely chopped),
@tomato paste{2%tsp}, @dried oregano{1/2%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp},
@granulated sugar{1/4%tsp} and @salt{1/4%tsp}, scraping up the browned bits.

Bring to a boil, then keep it at a gentle boil over medium, uncovered,
~{5%minutes}, until thickened.

Stir in the @parmesan{2%tbsp}(grated, or Pecorino Romano) and
@basil{2%tbsp}(chopped).

Return the chicken and its juices, turn the heat to low and simmer
~{1%minute} to ~{2%minutes}, until hot. Finish with more @basil{}.

> Using whole breasts? Halve them horizontally first, then pound to 1/8 to 1/4 inch.
